I couldn't get full coverage, and the spec says so where it matters:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Viewport sizes:
\f0\b0  the side panel limited the page to between 976 and 1126 wide, so I couldn't render it at 1440 or 390. I measured at 1126 (desktop layout) and 976 (phone layout). The 1440, 1024 and 390 sizes are worked out from the site's own fluid sizing rules and marked 
\f2\fs26 [inferred]
\f0\fs24 .\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Motion:
\f0\b0  the browser counted the tab as hidden, so animations only moved when I captured a frame. Most motion values come from the CSS and the scripts, which give exact numbers. I checked the hero entrance, the button hover and the page transition by capturing frames.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Load speed:
\f0\b0  the timings are from a cached reload, so they show what happens after the first visit. I couldn't measure when the largest image finished drawing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 What I found:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Loader:
\f0\b0  there isn't one. The hero text starts invisible until the fonts load, then drops in over 1.2 seconds. The background film is 18 MB.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Motion system:
\f0\b0  each section gets one "visible" class when it scrolls into view, and plain CSS transitions do the rest. Lines and buttons slide out from behind a hidden edge instead of fading in. In a group, everything starts at once but each item takes longer to arrive (+0.4s per line, +0.2s per card).\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Page transitions:
\f0\b0  the site uses the browser's built-in page transition. The old page shrinks and dims while the new one slides up, and the nav stays still.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Banned patterns:
\f0\b0  a "trusted by" line with a logo marquee under it, a scrolling wordmark in the footer, frosted cards, pill labels on news cards, an Intercom chat widget and a gated guidebook form. The site also has unused code for a text-scramble effect and a switched-off announcement bar. All are marked "do not copy".\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Error state:
\f0\b0  the /use-cases link in the Industries menu goes to a 404 page. I used it as the error state.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Light page:
\f0\b0  the brief tells Claude Code to use hurulab's palette and keep the page light, rather than copying Avalanche's dark background.\
